Suppose a universe of discourse is given, where {lo linji} is in a domain=
=20
of plural variable.
In this universe of discourse, {lo linji xi no} can be separated into=20
shorter {lo linji xi pany}:

lo linji xi pano cu me lo linji xi no
i
lo linji xi papa cu me lo linji xi no
i
...

Repeat the separation also for {lo linji xi pany}.
After infinite times of separation, {lo linji} is finally separated into=20
{lo mokca} which is individual:

RO DA poi ke'a me lo mokca zo'u lo mokca me DA

but for any shorter {lo linji}:

naku lo linji me lo mokca

Therefore, any {lo linji} does not satisfy=20
RO DA poi ke'a me lo linji zo'u lo linji me DA

{lo linji} in this universe of discourse is not an individual.

Please note that another universe of discourse can be given so that {lo=20
linji} is one or more individuals, but the selection of universe of=20
discourse depends on the epistemology of context, and cannot defined by the=
=20
language.

